{"step_index":1445,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-12T01:16:55Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-12T09:16:55+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-12T09:16:56+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-12T09:16:55+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-12T09:16:56+08:00\nShowing lines 1-19 of 19\n1: 1. For every changes Determine if a patch is a Major if so then must add a new subsequent patch entry following the previous patch number in `HISTORY.md`, For non-major patches, add the new changes below the current patch entry add why. Do not revise, replace, or update any of the existing patch details.\r\n2: 2. Do not build the APK. I will build it myself. YOU ARE PROHIBITED FROM TOUCHING/MODIFYING THE UNCODE ORIGINAL FILES OTHER THAN THE UI\r\n3: 3. Every update or proposed change must include a verification plan if the app works exactly as intended in the implementation_plan.md artifact across all Identify every file, class, component, or system behavior that directly or indirectly depends on the change, then specify how to verify that the app still works across those affected areas on devices. The verification must cover the changed file(s), their known dependents/callers, and any critical flow that could be affected and how do i verify those supposed flow or action still is working or is working.\r\n4: 4. SIREN HomeProxy is ONLY VIEWABLE; if YOU want to update it ask me anything explain why and what needs to be done\r\n5: 5. Always plan first after investigation use implementation plan(can always be edited regardless of any rule(any updates regarding implementation plan only negates rule 1)) is only for planning (not result of implementation)\r\n6: 6. You are not allowed to make any changes in any ocasions not until you ask me first plainly in text or if i clicked proceed with implementation plan.\r\n7: 7. **MANDATORY INVESTIGATION, RESEARCH & OPTIMIZATION:** For every requested code change, investigate the existing codebase and perform live web research relevant to the exact technologies, components, and problems involved before finalizing implementation decisions. Cross-reference the research with the existing implementation to identify the most efficient suitable algorithms, reduce time complexity where justified, minimize unnecessary memory allocations and CPU usage, eliminate duplicated logic and redundant execution paths, and enforce DRY. Optimization must preserve correctness, compatibility, and maintainability. Never fabricate research findings or performance improvements.\r\n8: 8. **MANDATORY EXECUTION WORKFLOW:** Every code modification or refactor must follow this sequence: (1) investigate the existing codebase and behavior; (2) perform live web research; (3) analyze dependencies, performance, and redundancy; (4) prepare the implementation plan, including affected files, proposed changes, optimization rationale, risks, and verification procedures; (5) stop and obtain my explicit approval under rule 6; (6) implement only the approved plan using workspace tools; and (7) verify the implementation and report actual results. Investigation and research may run concurrently, but implementation must never precede approval. The implementation plan is for planning only, not a record of completed work, and may be revised at any time without triggering rule 1.\r\n9: 9. **ABSOLUTE CODEBASE CONSTRAINTS:** Apply these requirements to every authorized modification:\r\n10:    - **ZERO IN-CODE DOCUMENTATION:** Do not introduce or leave comments, docstrings, TODO/FIXME notes, or explanatory plain-text documentation in modified code. Preserve necessary executable syntax and string literals. Do not modify unrelated files solely to remove existing comments.\r\n11:    - **CONTINUOUS ENFORCEMENT:** Aggressive optimization, redundancy elimination, documentation restrictions, and scope control apply throughout implementation and every subsequent edit.\r\n12: 10. **VERIFICATION & FINAL REPORT:** Follow rule 3 for every proposed and implemented change. Verify the modified files, known callers and dependents, and affected critical flows on relevant devices wherever testing is available. Use permitted tests and analysis without building an APK. Report the actual checks performed, results, failures, limitations, and anything that remains unverified. Never claim success without evidence.\r\n13: 11. **ADB PRIVILEGE PRIORITY:** Whenever ADB use is authorized, always prefer full available SU/root privileges or relevant built-in Custom ROM functions over standard ADB capabilities, even when standard ADB can accomplish the same task. Use whichever method is best suited to the task, and combine root privileges with Custom ROM functions when both are available and beneficial. If neither root access nor relevant Custom ROM functions are available, use standard ADB capabilities. You can even force stop/kill the app, Clear Logs at system or at kernel level if you want to see the issues further, basically anything you need to purge whatever issue it is.\r\n14: 12. **CRITICAL/SYSTEM FILE & LOG BACKUP:** When modifying, replacing, or deleting any system or critical OS file (local or on-device via ADB/root), create a timestamped backup directory at `C:\\AI Logs\\<DATE>\\<TIMESTAMP>\\` and follow this exact two-stage sequence:\r\n15:    - **Pre-Modification Target File Backup (BEFORE touching live files):**\r\n16:      - *Local Files:* Copy the untouched original file(s) into `C:\\AI Logs\\<DATE>\\<TIMESTAMP>\\files\\`, preserving the full relative directory structure to prevent filename collisions.\r\n17:      - *Android/ADB Files (under Rule 11):* Create an on-device backup in the same directory (`cp -a <file> <file>.bak`) to preserve exact UID/GID ownership, permissions, and SELinux contexts (`ls -Z`), AND pull a copy with its recorded `stat`/`ls -lZ` metadata to `C:\\AI Logs\\<DATE>\\<TIMESTAMP>\\files\\`.\r\n18:      - *Verification:* Verify that the target file backups exist and have a non-zero byte size matching the originals before modifying live system files. If the backup fails, abort immediately.\r\n19:    - **Post-Implementation Log Archival (ONLY AFTER executing the `implementation_plan.md` successfully):** Do not pre-backup session logs or plans. Once the implementation is completed and verified, copy the final `implementation_plan.md` and `.system_generated\\logs\\transcript.jsonl` in full from the active session directory (`C:\\Users\\Admin\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\<ACTIVE_SESSION_ID>\\`) into the same `C:\\AI Logs\\<DATE>\\<TIMESTAMP>\\` folder, along with a snippet of `.system_generated\\logs\\transcript_full.jsonl` saved as `transcript_full_snippet.jsonl` containing only the trailing entries for the completed task/turn. Verify these log files are non-zero before concluding the task.\n(no newline at end of file)"}
